  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.16,
      "text": "The chatbot responded with warmth, it even encouraged Sophie to seek help, but it had"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.16,
      "end": 9.44,
      "text": "no capacity to contact her family, alert her therapist, or bring a human into the room."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.14,
      "end": 13.92,
      "text": "After Sophie passed away, her mother described those chat logs as a black box."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.7,
      "end": 16.36,
      "text": "The AI offered empathetic words."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.18,
      "end": 22.8,
      "text": "But because those chats held crucial hidden details, they masked the severity of her distress"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.8,
      "end": 25.56,
      "text": "from the physical people around her who could have intervened."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.38,
      "end": 29.76,
      "text": "This panel outlines exactly what to do if someone may be in immediate danger."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.52,
      "end": 34.02,
      "text": "First, leave the chat. You need to tell a trusted adult or a school counselor."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.72,
      "end": 38.86,
      "text": "In the United States, call or text 988 for crisis support."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.6,
      "end": 42.1,
      "text": "If someone is in immediate danger, call 911."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.7,
      "end": 47.8,
      "text": "Second, do it now. Do not wait to perfect an explanation in a chat-"
    }
  ],
